{
  "notes": "Cinematic, C phrygian, 58 BPM, half-time and vast. Analog strings swelling in on long attacks in open voicings (root, fifth, octave, tenth), a detuned REESE drone underneath whose filter breathes on a slow LFO like distant machinery, the player's brass lead on the Smart Keys (the CZ brass made mono: glide, a slow delayed vibrato, long echoes), and an industrial kit far away: a deep thud, a metal gong at the phrase, a clank on the last bar. The phrygian half step (Db over C) is the tension everywhere. Scenes: A Cm and Db, each two bars, over their roots; B i VI II i with the drone holding C under the Ab (Ab/C) and stepping up to Db for the II; C the roots climb VI vii i III (Ab Bb C Eb) under pulsing strings and a heavy two-step bass; D the phrygian cadence II to i in a darker hall. ENERGY brings the drone, then the thuds and gongs, then the march and fills. All material is original.",
